Q: The &lt;map&gt; tag on the image does not work if it is loaded dynamically rather than directly in the HTML code A: <p>You can also use <code>createContextualFragment()</code> method...</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>let Dom_Frag = new Range().createContextualFragment(`
  &lt;img src="https://picsum.photos/id/691/400/300" usemap="#mymap"&gt;
  &lt;map name="mymap"&gt;
    &lt;area shape="circle" coords="316,226,50"&gt;
  &lt;/map&gt;`);

Dom_Frag.querySelector('area').addEventListener('click',e=&gt;
  {
  alert('this is not a coffee... (this a picture)');
  })

document.body.append(Dom_Frag);</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>map { cursor: pointer }</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;h2&gt; where is my coffee ? &lt;h2&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Why is the authorize attribute pointing to account/login? A: <p>You may want to simplify your configuration a bit by avoiding setting all default options.</p>
<p>Here's a working sample of an ASP.NET Core MVC application (<strong>.NET 8</strong>), where both Identity and Jwt are used and the default redirection url is overriden.</p>
<p><strong>Program.cs</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>builder.Services
    .AddIdentity&lt;ApplicationUser, IdentityRole&gt;()
    // ...

builder.Services
    .AddAuthentication()
    .AddCookie(CookieAuthenticationDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)
    .AddJwtBearer(JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme, options =&gt;
    {
        // ...
    });

builder.Services.ConfigureApplicationCookie(options =&gt; options.LoginPath = &quot;/Admin/Login&quot;);

// for the sake of sample completeness...
builder.Services.AddAuthorization(options =&gt;
{
    options.DefaultPolicy = new AuthorizationPolicyBuilder()
        .RequireAuthenticatedUser()
        .Build();
});
</code></pre>
<p><strong>In the controller</strong></p>
<pre><code>[Authorize(AuthenticationSchemes = &quot;Identity.Application&quot;)]
// or [Authorize]
// or no attribute if .RequireAuthorization() is applied globally to all endpoints
[HttpGet]
public IActionResult Index()
{
    // ...
}
</code></pre>
